From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:31:44 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 08/13] fix: run the Switch NRO under Ryujinx-based emulators

Astris (Ryujinx-based) starts an NRO with no argv at all, so the folder fell back to sdmc:/switch/ps2-web-recomp/ and the game was never found; it is now sdmc:/switch/<PS2_NRO_NAME>/. Threads created after SDL has brought up the GPU never start there either: the first std::thread or 32 MB allocation after that stalls, while a small NRO creates both kinds of thread fine. Until the render and VU threads move to cores of their own, the Switch runs everything on the main thread (PS2_ONE_THREAD).

Checked in Astris 1.0.14: Naruto Shippuden Ultimate Ninja 5 shows its language select, takes input and goes in game, very slowly with the software GS on one core. Headless (no SDL) it emulated 500 frames in 8 seconds there. Not run on a Switch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 1 +
 host/main.cpp  | 9 ++++++++-
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index db06dd5..8b03325 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -125,6 +125,7 @@ if(PS2_GENERATED)
     endif()
     if(NINTENDO_SWITCH)
         set(PS2_NRO_NAME "ps2-web-recomp" CACHE STRING "Title the homebrew menu shows for the NRO")
+        target_compile_definitions(ps2run PRIVATE PS2_NRO_DIR="sdmc:/switch/${PS2_NRO_NAME}/")
         nx_generate_nacp(ps2run.nacp NAME "${PS2_NRO_NAME}" AUTHOR "ps2-web-recomp")
         nx_create_nro(ps2run NACP ps2run.nacp)
     endif()
diff --git a/host/main.cpp b/host/main.cpp
index 6cb16a2..faab00a 100644
--- a/host/main.cpp
+++ b/host/main.cpp
@@ -34,12 +34,19 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv) {
 #ifdef __SWITCH__
     // Launched from the homebrew menu with no arguments: the game sits next to
     // the NRO as game.elf, disc.iso and memcard.ps2, and the log goes there too.
+    // Some loaders (the Ryujinx-based emulators) pass no argv[0] at all; then
+    // the folder is sdmc:/switch/<NRO name>/.
     std::vector<std::string> defaults;
     std::vector<char *> switch_argv;
     if (argc < 2) {
-        std::string dir = argc > 0 && argv[0] ? argv[0] : "sdmc:/switch/ps2-web-recomp/";
+        std::string dir = argc > 0 && argv[0] && std::strchr(argv[0], '/') ? argv[0] : PS2_NRO_DIR;
         dir = dir.substr(0, dir.find_last_of('/') + 1);
         std::freopen((dir + "ps2run.log").c_str(), "w", stderr);
+        std::setvbuf(stderr, nullptr, _IONBF, 0);
+        // Threads created after SDL has brought up the GPU never start under the
+        // Ryujinx-based emulators (malloc stalls); until the render and VU
+        // threads move to their own cores, emulation runs on the main thread.
+        setenv("PS2_ONE_THREAD", "1", 1);
         defaults = {"ps2run", dir + "game.elf", "--disc", dir + "disc.iso", "--memcard", dir + "memcard.ps2", "--window", "--fullscreen"};
         for (std::string &a : defaults) switch_argv.push_back(a.data());
         argc = static_cast<int>(switch_argv.size());
